    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, I'm Dr. Smith. It's nice to meet you; could you tell me what brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S012",
      "patient_response": "Hey Dr. Smith. Yeah, so, I came in because... man, I just feel like I’m literally crawling out of my skin whenever I’m supposed to sit still. Like in the radiology suite or in my classes. Which, honestly, the classes are crazy long. We had this one professor last week who brought in these physical bone models, and the room smelled so weird, kind of like dust and old chemicals? I don't know why they can't just use digital stuff, my laptop has this insane 3D program that renders everything way better. I built my PC myself, actually, got a new graphics card for it and everything so it runs super smooth. \n\nBut anyway, yeah, I've been trying to just tough it out for months now, but I just can't do it. I always end up pacing around the room, or just shifting in my chair constantly, or finding some random excuse to get up and move. Like I'll pretend I need to check the inventory in the supply closet... which is a total mess right now, by the way, someone left a bunch of contrast dye boxes right in the middle of the floor and I almost tripped over them on Tuesday...",
