    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Have you struggled with this kind of restlessness or difficulty sitting still since you were a child, or is this something that started more recently?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Oh, definitely since I was a kid. Like, my parents still talk about my elementary school parent-teacher conferences. The teachers were always complaining that I was constantly out of my seat, or calling out answers, or just rushing ahead before they even finished giving directions. \n\nWhich, honestly, I hate directions. Even now, if I buy something, I just look at the picture on the box and start building. I helped my buddy put together this TV stand last weekend, and he was trying to read the manual step-by-step, and I'm just like, dude, give me the screws, it's obvious. We actually ended up putting the back panel on backwards, but you can't even tell because it's against the wall. His apartment is so tiny anyway, and it's right next to the train tracks, so the whole place literally shakes when the freight trains go by at night. It's crazy loud. \n\nBut yeah, what was I saying? Oh, right, so this was happening way before middle school. It's definitely not just something that started recently with my radiology training.",
