    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Looking back at your childhood, would you say you frequently acted without thinking, such as blurting out answers in class or interrupting others while they were talking?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S016",
      "patient_response": "Yeah, oh man, all the time. Still do, honestly. Like, even now at the clinic, when a supervisor is explaining a positioning step for a scan, or asking me a question about the protocol, I’ll just jump in with the answer before they even finish talking. And then I realize I completely missed the part that actually mattered, because they were asking something else entirely. It's so embarrassing. \n\nBut it's just like... I know the answer! Or I think I do. It's like my brain is already ten steps ahead. Speaking of being ten steps ahead, I was trying to explain this new leveling system in this MMO I'm playing to my brother, and he just could not keep up. He plays a healer class, which I think is so boring. You just stand in the back and watch health bars go up and down. I have to play DPS, like a rogue or something, where I'm constantly moving and doing combos. If I'm not mashing buttons, I literally fall asleep at the keyboard. I actually spilled an entire energy drink on my mechanical keyboard last month because I fell asleep during a raid. It was a nightmare to clean. I had to take off every single keycap and swab the switches with rubbing alcohol. The alcohol smelled exactly like the prep wipes we use at the clinic before starting an IV... wait, what was the question? Did I answer it?",
